put('places.html','Three towns, four site ideas','A site-agnostic network across Dunwich (Goompi), Amity Point (Pulan) and Point Lookout (Mulumba).',
    hero('DISTRIBUTED ISLAND FACILITIES','Three towns. Several possible homes.',"Minjerribah's beaches change with storms and cyclones. A connected inland or reserve network could keep sand sport available, with each town taking a different role. None of these sites is approved for this proposal.",'site-ballow-aerial.webp')+
    section('DUNWICH (GOOMPI)','Two waterfront sites, different strengths','10-12 Ballow Road slopes toward the water beside QUAMPI and features in the Quandamooka Festival proposal. Its incline could make outdoor cinema dramatic, while courts, access and seating need careful grading. The former silica sand barge-loading area at the end of Cunningham Street is a separate, flatter waterfront option with wind exposure to design for. Neither site is selected or approved for Sandy Sports.',cards([
      ('BALLOW ROAD','10-12 Ballow Road candidate','Real aerial photo of the sloping waterfront block next to QUAMPI. The listing describes 7,727 m². Outdoor cinema could be spectacular here; sand sport and accessible routes must fit the grade.','site-ballow-aerial.webp','https://auraofintelligence.github.io/ballow-road-sand-screen-hub/site.html'),
      ('CUNNINGHAM STREET','Former sand barge loading area','Flat waterfront ground with potential for sand sport and events. Its usable area has not been measured here; boundaries, former industrial use, tenure, environmental history and wind exposure need investigation.','', '')],'two')+ballow_gallery,'alt')+
    section('AMITY POINT (PULAN)','Neighbourhood sport and club life','Explore the sports and recreation reserve without displacing the existing cricket field or current users. Sand courts, a shared clubhouse and night programmes are concepts to test with the land manager and community.',cards([('RESERVE','Amity Point (Pulan) sports and recreation reserve','A town foothold for recurring sessions, juniors, club crossover and adaptable event equipment.','','')]))+
    section('POINT LOOKOUT (MULUMBA)','A visitor-facing sports park','Explore the sports park opposite Point Lookout Bowls Club for court and event possibilities while respecting its existing uses. A beach sport venue there could connect residents, schools and visitors.',cards([('PARK','Point Lookout (Mulumba) sports park','Assess circulation, dimensions, nearby users, lighting, parking and a suitable shared facilities model.','','')]),'sunny')+
    section('RESILIENCE','A network matters when coastlines move','Permanent facilities can sit off the beach while portable sport and mobile screens reach seasonal and temporary locations. The three towns could specialise and still share equipment, bookings, coaches and events.','<div class="link-row"><a class="button coral" href="/space-planner.html">Test a footprint</a><a class="button outline" href="/facilities.html">See facility options</a></div>','dark'))

put('facilities.html','Facilities and infrastructure','A world-class adaptable facility programme for sports, events and three island towns.',
    hero('THE BUILT VISION','A sporting precinct that changes shape.','Design for multiple sand sports, night play, major events and daily community use. Choose fixed and movable elements for each site, then connect three towns with shared assets and operating agreements.','hero-trust.webp')+
    section('SPORT CORE','The sand and the game','Courts, larger fields, accessible paths and spectator circulation should be planned together. The surface specification, drainage, shade, net and goal systems, maintenance equipment and safe run-off depend on the sport and site.',cards([
      ('COURTS','Mixed volleyball campus','Multiple training and competition courts, adaptable for other net formats, with officials, seating and broadcast sightlines.','hero-sports.webp','/space-planner.html'),
      ('FIELDS','Larger sport zones','Separate configurable envelopes for beach cricket, football, flag and rugby variants rather than assuming a volleyball court fits all.','hero-sports.webp','/space-planner.html'),
      ('AFTER DARK','Lighting and power','Sports lighting, market and festival circuits, accessible routes and quiet-hour plans designed for neighbours and ecology.','hero-markets.webp','/assets.html')]),'alt')+
    section('CLUBHOUSE MODULES','Demountable, extendable and site-specific','Shipping-container-based modules could expand into reception, meeting rooms, storage, first aid, change and shower areas, film production support and food service. The final layout depends on site, building rules, water, wastewater, ventilation, heat and accessibility. Modules could move if the site needs change.',cards([
      ('PEOPLE','Dressing rooms and showers','Inclusive change spaces, family options, toilets, shade, drinking water and first aid sized to the programme.','hero-youth-elders.webp',''),
      ('OPERATIONS','Equipment and maintenance','Lockable sport gear, screen panels, tools, batteries, cleaning, inventory and vehicle access.','hero-funding.webp','/assets.html'),
      ('COMMUNITY','Meeting and media room','A flexible room for committee work, coaching, media training, film editing and club gatherings.','hero-film.webp','/film-club.html')]))+
    section('SCREEN SYSTEM','Permanent presence, mobile reach','A permanent outdoor LED screen on engineered support could anchor a major venue. Modular panels could also make smaller screens for clubs, travel between towns and support a managed hire programme. Screen safety, wind engineering, rigging, brightness, sound, power, rights, maintenance and storage need their own plan.','<div class="link-row"><a class="button coral" href="/film-club.html">Film club</a><a class="button outline" href="/assets.html">Asset wish list</a></div>','sunny'))

